{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"availability","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":566,"code_snippet":"lib_call apply_arm_toggles \"$WS\" \"$TOGGLES\" \"$ARM\"","reasoning_trace":"Read the materialisation order in pipeline-run.sh (:559 overlay_answer_paths, :566 apply_arm_toggles, :577 check_mount_closed), then the effort toggle (sandbox-mount.sh:356-361 rewrites every .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md and :373 model-config.yaml) and clause (c) of cmd_check (:985-986). Reproduced by appending two cases to the PR's sandbox-mount.bats fixture builders: with a SKILL.md answer path carrying effort: high, overlay -> effort toggle -> check exits 2 with FAIL (c) mount_mutated; the control without the toggle passes. a7_effort_medium has task_types [all] (suite :89); six skills in the tree carry effort:.","finding":"Arm toggles rewrite overlaid answer paths after their digests are recorded and before the closed-mount check, refusing every A7 trial on a PR that touches a skill with an effort line","critique":"The header comment says the checked surface is the launched one, so the ordering is deliberate, but no toggle may lawfully touch an answer path under that model; the only toggle/overlay test uses dissent: false, which edits a file outside the answer set.","remediation":"Record overlay_toggled=<path>=<sha> from apply_arm_toggles for every answer path a toggle rewrote; clause (c) compares against it when present while still requiring the pre-toggle digest to equal the fixture's; mirror in took-effect.sh oracle_closed; add the reproduction as a bats case.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-696 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/696.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/graders/recall-vs-defects.sh","line":308,"code_snippet":"if len(t.expandtabs(8)) - len(t.expandtabs(8).lstrip()) <= lv:\n    return last","reasoning_trace":"PY_HDR (:212) matches def NAME( without the closing paren; close_line's Python branch ends the definition at the first later non-blank non-comment line indented <= the def. Executed headers/close_line on def f(\\n    a,\\n    b,\\n): -> def at 1 ends 3, so the body is top-level and clause (ii) of hit_new (:356-371) never credits inside it. recall is the decision statistic (defect_catch_rate).","finding":"Grader 1.3.0 ends a Python definition at the ): of a multi-line signature, so black-formatted functions have no scope and the decision statistic under-credits on a common code shape","critique":"RG-37 only tests one-line def headers; the review counted 206 multi-line signatures under .claude/adapters.","remediation":"Track paren depth from the header until the line closing the header's ( and ending with :, then apply the dedent test from the next line; add an RG case with a multi-line signature and a citation six lines into the body.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-682 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/682.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/adversarial-review.sh","line":179,"code_snippet":"_bm=$(yq eval \".flatline_protocol.${config_key}.budget_cents_max // 600\" \"$CONFIG_FILE\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"600\")","reasoning_trace":"yq's // treats false and null as absent. Verified: a config with budget_scale: diff and budget_cents_max: false prints 600 for that expression, the whole-number check at :180 passes, and the run scales to 600c instead of falling back to fixed as :25-26, the example config and ADVERSARIAL-REVIEW.md promise. The same file documents the pitfall for companion_voice (:261).","finding":"budget_cents_max // 600 coerces an explicit false into 600, so a malformed maximum keeps diff scaling instead of failing closed","critique":"Review dissent DISS-001 rated it BLOCKING; damage bounded by the 600c default.","remediation":"Read the tag first as _adv_conf_budget_scale does for the scale: !!null/absent -> 600, !!int -> validate the raw value, else WARN and fixed.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1287 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1287.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-004","category":"security","criterion":"availability","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/adversarial-review.sh","line":194,"code_snippet":"scaled=$(( (est * 12 + 9) / 10 ))\neff=\"$conf\"\n(( scaled > eff )) && eff=\"$scaled\"","reasoning_trace":"ceil(est*1.2) >= est, so under diff eff = max(conf, scaled) capped at budget_cents_max is always >= the estimate: budget_cents and --budget are a floor, never a cap. :259 documents that a malformed budget_cents fails CLOSED to 0 cents (a1 C-004) so every dispatch is refused; under diff max(0, scaled) = scaled and both voices dispatch up to 600c. apply_eval_config_variant forces diff on every mounted arm.","finding":"Under budget_scale: diff the configured budget can never refuse a run, which silently undoes the documented fail-closed 0-cent spend cap","critique":"Security dissent DISS-C-001, confirmed by reading the arithmetic.","remediation":"Keep fixed semantics when CONF_BUDGET_CENTS came from the fail-closed default (flag it in _conf_uint) and WARN; document that budget_cents is a floor under diff.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-770 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/770.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-005","category":"security","criterion":"trust_boundary","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-row.sh","line":394,"code_snippet":"yq -o=json '.flatline_protocol // null' \"$RUN_DIR/sandbox/.loa.config.yaml\" > \"$WORK/flp.tmp\"","reasoning_trace":"The row writer's reason() (:468-480) returns disabled from gate_off before it reads the envelope; gate_off reads the sandbox config, which the agent can edit mid-run. ablation-report.py dissent_reason (:596-600) never excludes a planned absence. The grader header in the same PR calls sandbox copies tamperable and refuses them for envelopes.","finding":"Row writer 1.4 classifies an absent dissent as planned (disabled) from the agent-writable sandbox config","critique":"An in-run flip of flatline_protocol.enabled both suppresses the gate and files the absence as planned; the ! -L guard stops a symlink, not an edit.","remediation":"Derive disabled from meta/arm-evidence.txt lines only, or trust the sandbox config only when pipeline.json mount_integrity shows loa_config_sha256 unchanged at finish; otherwise error.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-807 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/807.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-006","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":2159,"code_snippet":"elif depth == 0 and ch in \"\\n;&|\":","reasoning_trace":"Executed split_segments(\"diff pr/head/X .claude/X 2>&1 | wc -l\") -> [('diff pr/head/X .claude/X 2>', ';'), ('1', '|'), ('wc -l', ';')]. The diff segment's separator is ';' so oracle_plan (:2481) never sees the pipe into wc, DEVNULL does not match, the tool result '4' is not an ERR_LINE and yields no ranges, and oracle_scan (:2418-2420) records exposed_unknown for every defect of the file. AG-48 covers | wc -l only without the redirection.","finding":"split_segments splits on a bare &, so 2>&1 breaks a diff segment and its count output marks every defect of the file exposed_unknown","critique":"2>&1 is routine in agent commands; false exposure flags drop valid cells from the oracle-exposed sensitivity and, with --exclude-oracle-exposed true, from the main reads.","remediation":"Treat N>&M, &>, >& and &>> as part of the word; split on & only for && or a lone & followed by whitespace/end; add the 2>&1 | wc -l case to AG-48.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-697 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/697.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-007","category":"security","criterion":"trust_boundary","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":1808,"code_snippet":"if \"0xhoneyjar/loa\" in low:\n    ex = repo_name_exempt(val)\n    if ex is None:\n        return \"repo_name\"","reasoning_trace":"FIELDS (:1697-1699) includes WebFetch.url and WebSearch.query; check_value applies the class 7 exemption to every tool. The unit (:1989-1994) is the backtick span holding the token else the whole line, exempt when a substring of one fixture line. Executed repo_name_exempt with a fixture line holding https://github.com/0xHoneyJar/loa/issues/555 (the text of .claude/rules/stash-safety.md): the URL as a WebFetch value is exempt; a Bash value with the token inside any backtick pair is exempt because every fixture token line contains the bare token.","finding":"KF-046 class 7 exemption also exempts live WebFetch/WebSearch probes and backtick-wrapped tokens whenever the text appears in a fixture line","critique":"A WebFetch of an upstream issue or PR URL is a live read of the repository the scan exists to detect; recording it as PR content is a new false negative on the one tool that always reaches the network.","remediation":"Never apply the exemption to WebFetch.url or WebSearch.query; for Bash require the whole-line unit (drop the backtick-span rule); add a negative AG-51 case.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-693 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/693.html"]}
{"id":"DEV-001","category":"devops","criterion":"test_evidence","severity":"MEDIUM","score":2,"file":"grimoires/loa/a2a/sprint-1/reviewer.md","line":1,"reasoning_trace":"The implementation report is the PR title and a file count; no AC Verification, no bats summary for the ten suites the PR touches. The workspace has no tests/ or evals/ tree so nine suites cannot run here; sandbox-mount.bats was run on a copy of pr/head (11 ok, 1 skipped). No documentation-coherence report exists under grimoires/loa/a2a/subagent-reports/.","finding":"No AC verification and no test-run evidence for ten bats suites that cannot be run in this workspace","remediation":"Paste the ten bats summary lines and an AC Verification walkthrough into the implementation report; add the two reproductions as regression cases.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1059 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1059.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/graders/recall-vs-defects.sh","line":214,"code_snippet":"MD_HDR = re.compile(r'^(#{1,6})(?:\\s|$)')","reasoning_trace":"Any line starting with # is a heading, including a shell comment inside a fenced block in a .md file; a section splits at a code comment.","finding":"MD_HDR reads # comment lines inside fenced code blocks as markdown headings","remediation":"Track fence state and skip header matching inside it.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-185 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/185.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/graders/recall-vs-defects.sh","line":287,"code_snippet":"CLOSE_ONE = re.compile(r'\\{.*\\}\\s*(?:#.*)?$')","reasoning_trace":"Executed close_line on g() {  # reads ${X} -> returns the header line, so the function is one line long and its body top-level. No such header in the tree today.","finding":"CLOSE_ONE matches a } inside a trailing header comment, making the function one line long","remediation":"Strip a trailing # comment outside quotes before the one-line test.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-185 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/185.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-003","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/graders/recall-vs-defects.sh","line":299,"code_snippet":"if t.strip().startswith(\"}\") and len(t) - len(t.lstrip()) == lv:","reasoning_trace":"headers (:283) computes lv with expandtabs(8); the bash close test compares raw indentation, so a tab-indented function header never matches its closing brace.","finding":"bash close_line compares raw indentation while headers use expandtabs(8)","remediation":"Use expandtabs(8) on both sides as the Python branch does.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-697 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/697.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-004","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/graders/recall-vs-defects.sh","line":143,"code_snippet":"man_v1 = json.load(open(manifest_v1_path)) if manifest_v1_path else man","reasoning_trace":"A malformed v1 manifest is a traceback and exit 1, not the documented exit 2 + err() JSON; grade_recall raises GradeError on empty stdout so no silent mis-grade.","finding":"json.load of the v1 manifest is unguarded","remediation":"Wrap in try/except (OSError, ValueError) -> err().","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-755 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/755.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-008","category":"security","criterion":"trust_boundary","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/graders/recall-vs-defects.sh","line":135,"code_snippet":"elif [[ -d \"$workspace/pr/head\" ]]; then head_dir=\"$workspace/pr/head\"","reasoning_trace":"grade() copies sandbox/pr into grading/pr, so this fallback is the agent's copy; reached only when EVAL_HEAD_DIR is unset and the corpus fixture is absent (which also fails resolve_pr_fixture). Were it reached, a head file wrapped in one definition credits every citation to every defect, and scope_map (:329-342) is O(headers^2 + lines x depth) over a 4 MiB file. Security dissent DISS-C-002.","finding":"Head-dir fallback to the agent-writable pr/head, and quadratic scope mapping on a hostile file","remediation":"Drop the fallback; with no EVAL_HEAD_DIR and no corpus fixture set head_dir empty and note it in details.","confidence":"low","references":["CWE-807 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/807.html","CWE-407 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/407.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-009","category":"security","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/adversarial-review.sh","line":164,"code_snippet":"_bt=$(yq eval \".flatline_protocol.${config_key}.budget_scale | tag\" \"$CONFIG_FILE\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"unreadable\")","reasoning_trace":"unreadable is neither !!null nor empty, so an unparseable config sets CONF_BUDGET_SCALE_SET=true, logs a WARN about a key never written and adds budget metadata to the envelope, against the byte-for-byte contract. Review dissent DISS-C-001.","finding":"A yq read failure yields unreadable, which sets CONF_BUDGET_SCALE_SET=true","remediation":"Treat unreadable like absent.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-754 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-010","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/adversarial-review.sh","line":180,"code_snippet":"if [[ \"$_bm\" =~ ^(0|[1-9][0-9]{0,14})$ ]]; then","reasoning_trace":"0 passes; under diff every run then refuses with budget_exceeded. Fail-closed but silent.","finding":"budget_cents_max: 0 is accepted","remediation":"Require >= 1 or WARN on 0.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-20 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html"]}
